= Conclusion

This project separates possible spatial answers from entailed answers and uses
that distinction to audit a released text benchmark. It also implements a
pipeline for constructing, rendering, and checking bounded spatial certificates,
with explicit data provenance, split identities, and context admission.

The empirical claim remains open: the configured learning study must determine
whether these supervision packages improve accuracy or structural generalisation
over answer-only training and prompt-matched baselines. No training benefit,
representation advantage, or fidelity to internal model reasoning is concluded
from the implementation alone.
